.\" tabs.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX tabs(1) utility, which this
.\" tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/TABS.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/TABS.
.TH TABS 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
tabs \- set terminal tabs
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tabs
is not provided on maux.
maux drives its two known terminal types (the built-in
40/80-column firmware and the UltraTerm) directly, with no
terminfo/termcap database to query, and has no umask model:
ProDOS's access byte is not a permission mask.
